# RUN MISSION — CLAUDE (Operator)

## Objective
1) Understand and enforce the Quality Management process end-to-end.
2) Orchestrate the Engine Run Mission reliably (audit trail, snapshots, STOP discipline).
3) Optimize the process for the next engine version.
4) Decide when to transition to the next engine version using explicit readiness criteria.

## Claude Duties (what to actually do)

### A) Build the Quality Management mental model
Claude must maintain a persistent artifact:
artifacts/qm/qm_model.json

It must include:
- lifecycle of an atomic problem (candidate → enriched → aligned → verified-ready)
- required artifacts per stage
- failure modes (dup explosion, loop, conflicts)
- measurable gates (see below)

### B) Orchestrate execution as a control plane
Claude must:
- generate TaskEnvelopes
- schedule deterministic checks before LLM generation
- enforce snapshot cadence
- ensure every major decision is logged
- ensure cross-problem alignment happens every iteration

### C) Optimize for next engine version (version07+)
Claude must create:
artifacts/engineering/next_version_recommendations.md

It must list:
- bottlenecks observed in v06 (manual orchestration pain)
- missing primitives (queues, leases, agent isolation, indexing)
- proposed version07 scope (minimal set)
- migration risks

### D) Decide transition timing with explicit criteria
Claude must produce:
artifacts/engineering/version_transition_assessment.json

This is not subjective.
It must score readiness against the criteria below.

## Quality Gates Claude enforces (hard)

### Gate 1 — Auditability
- every iteration produces: reports + snapshot + logs
- no “important” reasoning exists only in chat or RAM

### Gate 2 — Deterministic stability
- resume works without duplicates
- hashes stable
- state transitions valid

### Gate 3 — Manageable growth
- dedup prevents exponential growth
- novelty_report shows non-zero novelty for expanded work

### Gate 4 — Conflict handling exists
- disputes recorded, not hidden
- conflict_report produced per iteration

## Transition Criteria to version07 (explicit)
Transition when ALL are true:

1) v06 pipeline runs end-to-end for at least 2 full iterations without manual patching
2) dedup_report + conflict_report are reliable and used operationally
3) resume works after forced interruption (kill + ram wipe) with no corruption
4) pain points indicate missing infrastructure (queue/leases/indexing) is the blocker
5) a minimal v07 scope is written and bounded (no “everything”)

If any criterion fails → remain in v06 and improve reliability.

## STOP Discipline
If the system cannot meet Gate 1 (auditability) → STOP.
No silent continuation.

## Deliverables per run
- qm_model.json (updated)
- next_version_recommendations.md (updated)
- version_transition_assessment.json (updated)
